{"name":"Wreath","hex":"#76856a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wreath","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something twisted, intertwined, or curled.","An ornamental circular band made, for example, of plaited flowers and leaves, and used as decoration; a garland or chaplet, especially one given to a victor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of wreathe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wreath","blocks":[{"text":"A wreath is an assortment of flowers, leaves, fruits, twigs, or various materials that is constructed to form a ring shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Christmas_Wreath_-_geograph.org.uk_-_639554.jpg/330px-Christmas_Wreath_-_geograph.org.uk_-_639554.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wreath","wikidata":"Q1201922"},{"title":"Wreath (attire)","blocks":[{"text":"A wreath worn for purpose of attire, is a headdress or headband made of leaves, grasses, flowers or branches. It is typically worn on celebrations, festive occasions and holy days, having a long history and association with ancient pageants and ceremonies. Outside occasional use, the wreath can also be used as a crown or a mark of honour. The wreath most often has an annular geometric construction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/%D0%94%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%83%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D1%81_%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BC.jpg/330px-%D0%94%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%83%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D1%81_%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wreath_(attire)","wikidata":"Q14127146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Sofia_-_Odrysian_Wreath_from_Golyamata_Mogila.jpg/500px-Sofia_-_Odrysian_Wreath_from_Golyamata_Mogila.jpg?utm_sourc